    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 080930\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n130 AM PST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Quiet and pleasant conditions anticipated through Friday.\n\n* Models continue to suggest the return of an active pattern by next \n  weekend.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through next weekend.\n\nUpper-level ridging largely remains in place this week, with just \nsome slight fluctuations as a weak disturbance passes through mid-\nweek. During this time, temperatures stay 2-6 degrees above normal, \nresulting in quite pleasant weather across the region. Some periodic \nbreeziness is possible mid-week, but not expecting anything \nimpactful. Precipitation chances remain below 10% through Friday \nafternoon. \n\nLate in the week, the pattern becomes more active with a closed low \nset to develop off the SoCal/Baja coast and a larger trough in the \nnortheast Pacific. Guidance is coming into better agreement on the \nplacement and phasing (or lack thereof in this case) of these \nsystems. Latest runs have the closed low coming ashore late Friday \nand into the weekend. There remains a fair amount of track \nuncertainty, but the southern track shown in most guidance results \nin low (10-30%) PoPs across the southern half of the CWA Friday \nnight into Saturday with limited temperature and wind response. As \nfor the larger trough, timing looks most likely to be late in the \nweekend and into the following week. Uncertainty is still moderate \nto high, but this second system looks more favorable for widespread \nprecipitation, cooler temperatures, and increased winds.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Light\nwinds under 8KT will follow typical daily directional patterns, \nshifting from the southwest to northeast by late morning, then \nveering to the west early evening. VFR conditions with clear skies\nwill continue.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Northerly terrain-\nenhanced winds continue through the Lower Colorado River Valley from \nKIFP to KEED, with the strongest winds expected at KIFP where gusts \nto around 20KT return by mid- morning and persist into the \nafternoon. Elsewhere, winds follow typical daily directional \npatterns with speeds around 5-10KT. Gusty up-valley winds in the \nnorthern Owens Valley could produce intermittent gusts to around \n15KT at KBIH during the afternoon, diminishing by mid-evening. VFR \nconditions prevail.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Woods\nAVIATION...Phillipson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
